[115.8985, "o", "PR watch check at Wed, Nov 11, 18:31 EST; nothing was written: new problems, so the shepherd would start a run scoped to them.\r\n- #11 (head 4595c1b): merge conflict; 1 failed check (1 new); review waits until the merge conflict is resolved\r\n\r\nPrompt section the run would get:\r\n\r\n## Triggered run (PR watch): read first\r\nThe PR watch started this run at Wed, Nov 11, 18:31 EST because it found problems the shepherd hasn't been given yet. This is not a regular run.\r\n\r\n- PR #11 (https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11), branch `orka-demo/quantity-parser`, head `4595c1b`:\r\n  - It has a merge conflict with its base branch (mergeable: CONFLICTING).\r\n  - These checks failed, and CI on this head has finished:\r\n    - Trigger CI Approval Flow / ok-to-test: FAILURE (https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/actions/runs/43117441162/job/130848956275)\r\n\r\nScope of this run:\r\n- Work only on the PRs listed above, and only on the problems listed: step A (rebase) for a merge conflict, step B (CI) for failed checks. Re-triage those PRs"]
[115.8985, "o", " first, because their state may have changed since the watch looked. If a problem is already gone, say so and leave that PR alone.\r\n- Skip steps C-G (CodeRabbit, human reviews, approvals, codeowner pings, and age). The regular runs cover them.\r\n- Every other rule below still applies, including backups, validation, the per-run limits, and signed, signed-off commits. Start the report with \"Triggered by the PR watch:\" and the problems above.\r\n"]
[119.8985, "m", "4. A demo schedule pointed at the fork"]
