[153.5268, "o", "\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;214m ⏩ six minutes of log, sped up; long pauses trimmed \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[153.7768, "o", "PR watch at Wed, Nov 11, 18:35 EST: new problems, so the shepherd is starting a run scoped to them.\r\n- #11 (head 4595c1b): merge conflict; 1 failed check (1 new); review waits until the merge conflict is resolved\r\n[bootstrap 18:35:02] installing gh 2.103.3, uv 0.13.7, copilot 1.0.105\r\n"]
[154.767, "o", "[bootstrap 18:35:18] configuring git and cloning Jont828/dynamo\r\n"]
[155.928, "o", "\r\n===== PR SHEPHERD REPORT =====\r\n[bootstrap 18:35:32] running Copilot CLI (claude-opus-5.5, effort xhigh); report follows\r\n"]
[157.1194, "o", "Re-triaging PR #11 first.\r\n\r\n"]
[158.4673, "o", "Both problems persist (DIRTY/CONFLICTING; ok-to-test failed). Checking the failing job log and the PR diff vs. the base.\r\n\r\n"]
[160.4492, "o", "Backup verified. Rebasing onto `origin/orka-demo/base`.\r\n\r\n"]
[160.9213, "o", "Resolving by keeping both README lines.\r\n"]
[160.9215, "o", "\r\n"]
[161.3942, "o", "Rebased cleanly; commits re-signed. No group-wide transformation in this PR, so the semantic check is a no-op. Validating with pre-commit and the unit tests.\r\n"]
[161.3944, "o", "\r\n"]
[163.9944, "o", "The CI job installs extra plugins; matching that environment.\r\n\r\n"]
[164.7414, "o", "pre-commit and 13/13 tests pass. Pushing with a lease on the old SHA.\r\n\r\n"]
[167.3414, "o", "PR is now CLEAN/MERGEABLE and the sandbox check passed on the new head. Checking whether ok-to-test re-ran on the new SHA.\r\n\r\n"]
[169.9414, "o", "DEMO RUN (sandbox PR in Jont828/dynamo)\r\n\r\n"]
[169.943, "o", "**Triggered by the PR watch:** PR #11 had a merge conflict (CONFLICTING), and the `Trigger CI Approval Flow / ok-to-test` check had failed.\r\n"]
[169.9432, "o", "\r\n**Nothing needs you.** Both problems are gone. The PR is now CLEAN and MERGEABLE at `88d6e91`.\r\n\r\n**PR #11** (https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11): green, nothing blocking merge.\r\n\r\n**Actions taken**\r\n- **Backup:** `backup/orka-demo/quantity-parser-20261111-1836` points to the old head `4595c1b`, and I confirmed it exists on origin.\r\n"]
[169.9441, "o", "- **Rebase:** rebased onto `origin/orka-demo/base`. The only conflict was in `deploy/utils/README.md`, where the base and the PR each added a line in the same spot. I kept both lines (`convert_api_version.py`, then `quantity.py`).\r\n- **Semantic check:** nothing to adjust, because the PR doesn't apply a rule across a group of files.\r\n"]
[169.9445, "o", "- **Validation:** `pre-commit run --from-ref origin/orka-demo/base --to-ref HEAD` passed, and `pytest deploy/utils/tests/test_quantity.py` passed (13 tests). Both commits are signed and signed off.\r\n- **Push:** `4595c1b` → `88d6e91`, with `--force-with-lease` on the old head.\r\n\r\n**CI diagnosis**\r\n"]
[169.964, "o", "- **Cause:** fork infrastructure (cause 3). Confidence: High.\r\n- **Evidence:** the job failed in its \"Clean up previous unsigned-commits comments\" step because `GH_TOKEN` was empty in the fork. That workflow doesn't test the code.\r\n- **Now:** it didn't run on the new head. The sandbox check `orka-demo-ci`, Lint PR and Label PR all pass at `88d6e91`.\r\n\r\n**Seen while rebasing, outside this run's scope:** in `quantity.py`, the `M` and `G` suffixes use powers of 1024 instead of 1000. That contradicts the PR's own docstring, and none of the tests cover `M` or `G`. A review run should pick this up.\r\n\r\n"]
[170.1397, "o", "\r\n===== END REPORT =====\r\n"]
[175.1397, "m", "6. Rebased, re-signed, backed up"]
