[214.062, "o", "\u001b[48;5;236m\u001b[38;5;214m ⏩ nine minutes of log, sped up; long pauses trimmed \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[214.312, "o", "PR watch at Wed, Nov 11, 18:41 EST: a review is due, so the shepherd is starting a review run.\r\n- #11 (head 88d6e91): no merge conflict; CI passed (4 checks); review due (full review)\r\n[bootstrap 18:41:08] installing gh 2.103.3, uv 0.13.7, copilot 1.0.105\r\n"]
[214.6933, "o", "[bootstrap 18:41:22] configuring git and cloning Jont828/dynamo\r\n"]
[215.5479, "o", "\r\n[bootstrap 18:41:34] running Copilot CLI (claude-opus-5.5, effort xhigh); report follows\r\n===== PR SHEPHERD REPORT =====\r\n"]
[216.528, "o", "I'll start by fetching remotes and triaging PR #11.\r\n\r\n"]
[218.2859, "o", "PR is CLEAN, CI green, no approvals. Now pulling the CodeRabbit review body and review threads.\r\n\r\n"]
[218.6642, "o", "One unresolved CodeRabbit thread (M/G multipliers). Let me read the PR's code at head and the base diff.\r\n\r\n"]
[220.229, "o", "CodeRabbit's finding still applies at head (`M`/`G` use 1024). Next, I'll read the review rubric from upstream/main for self-review.\r\n\r\n"]
[221.9031, "o", "Rubric read. Now checking test markers, CI collection, replication (existing quantity parsers / `kubernetes.utils.parse_quantity`), and running the tests.\r\n\r\n"]
[222.685, "o", "The test run needs the same deps CI installs; installing them into the venv.\r\n\r\n"]
[223.8283, "o", "13 tests pass at head. Now reproducing the CodeRabbit claim and probing edge cases against Kubernetes semantics.\r\n\r\n"]
[226.2283, "o", "Verifying the new tests fail without the fix and pass with it, then running pre-commit.\r\n\r\n"]
[226.6029, "o", "Regression tests fail without the fix and pass with it. Running pre-commit on the PR's files.\r\n\r\n"]
[229.0029, "o", "Pre-commit passes. Before committing, a fresh subagent will confirm the diff fixes exactly the listed item and nothing else.\r\n"]
[229.003, "o", "\r\n"]
[231.403, "o", "**CONFIRMED**\r\n\r\n"]
[231.4175, "o", "- **(a)** `/tmp/work/dynamo/deploy/utils/quantity.py` changes only `M` and `G` to `1000**2` and `1000**3`, matching Kubernetes decimal semantics.\r\n"]
[231.4376, "o", "- **(b)** New `M`/`G` assertions pass with current source: **15 passed**. With old multipliers, all three new assertions fail with `1048576`/`1073741824`.\r\n"]
[231.4618, "o", "- **(c)** Diff contains only those multiplier fixes and regression assertions. Other suffixes are unchanged; `git diff --check` passes.\r\n\r\n"]
[231.8229, "o", "No problem found in the diff. The normal pytest command initially loaded a stale same-second `.pyc`; forcing current source confirmed the passing result.Confirmed. Re-checking the PR head and approvals, then committing (signed, signed-off) and pushing.\r\n\r\n"]
[232.5893, "o", "Commit is signed and signed off. Running pre-commit over the full PR range, then pushing with a lease on the old head.\r\n\r\n"]
[234.3615, "o", "Pushed `418a77b`. Now replying in the CodeRabbit thread and resolving it.\r\n\r\n"]
[235.5243, "o", "Thread resolved. Waiting for CI on the new head before writing the brief.\r\n\r\n"]
[237.1744, "o", "CI is green at `418a77b`. Posting the review brief (none exists yet).\r\n\r\n"]
[238.4545, "o", "I'll write the brief with literal values instead of shell substitution.\r\n\r\n"]
[239.123, "o", "Brief posted. Final state check and cleanup.\r\n\r\n"]
[240.1206, "o", "DEMO RUN (sandbox PR in Jont828/dynamo)\r\n\r\n"]
[240.1221, "o", "**Triggered by the PR watch:** CodeRabbit's review of PR #11 (`orka-demo/quantity-parser`, head `88d6e91`), so I did a full review.\r\n\r\n**Nothing needs you.** Two optional nits for you are at the end.\r\n\r\n### [PR #11](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11): Kubernetes quantity parser\r\n**Status:** Merge state is CLEAN, all checks pass at `418a77b`, there are no approvals, and every review thread is resolved. It didn't need a rebase.\r\n\r\n**What I did**\r\n"]
[240.124, "o", "- **CodeRabbit's finding was right.** The `M` and `G` suffixes used powers of 1024, so `\"1M\"` came out as 1048576 instead of 1000000. I switched both to powers of 1000 and added tests for `1M`, `1G` and `memory_bytes(\"1G\")`. All three new tests fail on the old code.\r\n- **Pushed** that fix as `418a77b`, a signed and signed-off commit. No backup branch was needed because the push only added a commit.\r\n- **Validation:** the 15 tests pass, pre-commit is clean, and the sandbox test check passed at the new head.\r\n- **Thread:** I replied with the commit and resolved it.\r\n- **Review brief:** [posted](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11#issuecomment-6810034200). It rates the risk Low and asks reviewers one question: nothing calls the module yet, so should it merge now or land with its first caller?\r\n\r\n"]
[240.1241, "o", "**Review totals:** 1 fixed, 0 declined, 0 refuted, 0 pre-existing. My own review found nothing serious beyond CodeRabbit's issue.\r\n\r\n**Optional nits for you**\r\n"]
[240.1242, "o", "1. The parser rejects `1.` and `+1`, which Kubernetes accepts. A test rejects `-1`, so leaving out signs looks deliberate. Either widen the pattern or say so in the module docstring.\r\n"]
[240.1318, "o", "2. The PR description doesn't give the core-logic line count (about 25 lines) under Key Changes. It also doesn't record that a search found no existing parser, not even in `kubernetes-asyncio`. The `pr-checklist` skill asks for both.\r\n\r\n"]
[240.2523, "o", "\r\n===== END REPORT =====\r\n"]
