[270.3486, "o", "Jont828 · 2026-11-11T23:49:19Z · https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11#issuecomment-6810034200\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-shepherd:review-brief head=418a77b3f27b7810d179a21a7d253aa171f92a76 -->\r\n**Review brief** for 418a77b, written by the author's automated PR assistant.\r\n\r\n**What it does:** Adds `deploy/utils/quantity.py`, a stdlib-only parser that turns Kubernetes CPU \r\nand memory quantities (`500m`, `512Mi`, `1G`) into `Decimal`, with millicore and byte helpers and \r\nunit tests.\r\n"]
[270.3487, "o", "**Risk:** Low. It's a new standalone module with about 25 lines of logic and no callers yet. It \r\ndoesn't touch core components, user-facing contracts, CI, or build or deploy files.\r\n**Where to look:**\r\n1. \r\n[`deploy/utils/quantity.py#L27-L40`](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/blob/418a77b3f27b7810d179a21\r\na7d253aa171f92a76/deploy/utils/quantity.py#L27-L40): the suffix table and regex. The accepted \r\ngrammar is a deliberate subset of Kubernetes': no exponents, no `P`/`E`, no signs.\r\n2. \r\n[`deploy/utils/tests/test_quantity.py`](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/blob/418a77b3f27b7810d179\r\na21a7d253aa171f92a76/deploy/utils/tests/test_quantity.py): decimal vs. binary suffixes, rounding, \r\nand rejected input.\r\n\r\n**Decisions for reviewers:**\r\n1. Nothing calls this module yet. Merge it now as a standalone utility, or land it together with \r\nits first caller in the benchmarking tooling? (`kubernetes-asyncio`, which `deploy/utils` already \r\nuses, has no quantity parser, so a small local one avoids adding the sync `ku"]
[270.3487, "o", "bernetes` client.)\r\n\r\n**Checked:** `deploy-utils unit tests` passed at 418a77b. `pytest \r\ndeploy/utils/tests/test_quantity.py` passes (15 tests) and `pre-commit run --from-ref \r\n"]
[270.3487, "o", "origin/orka-demo/base` is clean. CodeRabbit: 1 fixed in 418a77b (`M`/`G` were powers of 1024; \r\n"]
[270.3487, "o", "regression tests added), 0 declined. Self-review: no further P0–P2 findings.\r\n**Still open:** Nothing.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Declined CodeRabbit suggestions (0)</summary>\r\n"]
[270.3487, "o", "\r\nNone.\r\n"]
[270.3487, "o", "</details>\r\n"]
[270.3487, "o", "\r\n"]
