[309.5187, "o", "DEMO RUN (sandbox PR in Jont828/dynamo)\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "**Triggered by the PR watch:** CodeRabbit's review of PR #11 (`orka-demo/quantity-parser`, head \r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "`88d6e91`), so I did a full review.\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "**Nothing needs you.** Two optional nits for you are at the end.\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "### [PR #11](https://github.com/Jont828/dynamo/pull/11): Kubernetes quantity parser\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "**Status:** Merge state is CLEAN, all checks pass at `418a77b`, there are no approvals, and every \r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "review thread is resolved. It didn't need a rebase.\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "**What I did**\r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "- **CodeRabbit's finding was right.** The `M` and `G` suffixes used powers of 1024, so `\"1M\"` came \r\n"]
[309.5187, "o", "out as 1048576 instead of 1000000. I switched both to powers of 1000 and added tests for `1M`, \r\n"]
[313.4187, "o", "\r\n\u001b[38;5;39m\u001b[1mh100\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;245m~/orka-demo\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;214m❯\u001b[0m "]
